      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since this property is never going to be set everywhere, doesn\u0027t this lock the majority of the platform into the set of warnings that currently exist, plus whichever new ones get cleaned up in the tree so they can be enabled globally?  How is this better than the current system, where we just globally disable any problematic warnings?  This would seem more useful if it returned config.CurrentClangDiagnosticVersion if it was unset, and then you can pin problematic modules to an older version.",
